1
00:00:00,420 --> 00:00:03,563
Euclid's Elements, Book One, Proposition Thirty.

2
00:00:03,563 --> 00:00:07,820
Lines parallel to the same line are also parallel to one another.

3
00:00:07,820 --> 00:00:12,012
Let each of the segments A B and C D be parallel to segment E F.

4
00:00:12,012 --> 00:00:15,810
We prove that segment A B is also parallel to segment C D.

5
00:00:16,230 --> 00:00:23,120
Let transversal segment G K fall upon segments A B, E F, and C D at points G, H, and K.

6
00:00:23,540 --> 00:00:32,921
Since segment G K falls on parallel segments A B and E F, by Proposition Twenty-Nine, alternate interior angles A G K and G H F are equal.

7
00:00:32,921 --> 00:00:43,186
Again, since segment G K falls on parallel segments E F and C D, by Proposition Twenty-Nine, exterior angle G H F equals opposite interior angle G K D.

8
00:00:43,186 --> 00:00:50,867
By Common Notion One, things equal to the same thing are equal to one another, so angle A G K equals angle G K D.

9
00:00:50,867 --> 00:01:00,180
Since these are alternate interior angles, by Proposition Twenty-Seven, segment A B is parallel to segment C D, as was required to prove.
